# Gustav Mattsson — Personal Design System

A personal design system for Gustav Mattsson — a designer/developer whose
mark is the binary string **0100 0111** (= ASCII `G`) paired with a
hand-drawn paintbrush. The system pairs that quiet, technical foundation
with playful, hand-drawn accents.

## Brand assets

Final assets live in `assets/` and `fonts/`:

| File | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `assets/logo-black.png` | Primary logo (black — for light backgrounds) |
| `assets/logo-white.png` | Inverse logo (white — for dark backgrounds) |
| `assets/gustav-portrait.jpg` | Personal portrait, B&W |
| `fonts/Montserrat-VariableFont_wght.ttf` | Display + body type |
| `fonts/Montserrat-Italic-VariableFont_wght.ttf` | Italic axis |
| `fonts/PatrickHand-Regular.ttf` | Hand-drawn accent type |

The mark is the binary **0100 0111** (= ASCII `G`) beside a hand-drawn
paintbrush. Color: Ember palette (coral `#FF582D` + teal `#3AA59C` on
neutral grey); see `colors_and_type.css`.

> No codebase, Figma, or product copy was supplied. The content
> fundamentals and the personal-site UI kit are an **inferred
> proposal** for a one-person *personligt designsystem* — refine the
> voice/copy against real material when you have it.

---

## CONTENT FUNDAMENTALS

The brand voice is **first-person, calm, confident, playful**. The
binary "G" hints at engineering rigor; the Patrick Hand accents and red
brushstroke hint at warmth and a maker's touch. Hold both at once.

### Voice

- **First-person, singular.** "I", "my", "me" — this is one person, not a
  studio.
- **You, not we.** Address the reader directly: "you'll see…", "let me
  show you…".
- **Plain Swedish/English.** Short sentences. No corporate hedging. No
  buzzwords ("synergy", "ecosystem", "leverage" — never).
- **Confident but warm.** "Here's what I made." Not "We are excited to
  announce…".
- **Specific over abstract.** "Three days, no Figma, just a notebook"
  beats "an iterative design process".

### Tone

| Context | Register |
| --- | --- |
| Hero / intro | Quiet, declarative. One sentence. |
| Project case study | Storytelling, past tense, "I tried X, then Y". |
| Microcopy / buttons | Verbs only. "Open", "Get in touch", "Read more". |
| 404 / errors | Self-aware, hand-drawn note. "Hmm, det här finns inte." |

### Casing

- **Sentence case** for headings and buttons. Not Title Case. Not
  ALL CAPS (except the eyebrow/kicker token, which is uppercase + tracked
  for typographic rhythm).
- **Lowercase i** in standalone "i" outside sentences is fine in Swedish
  contexts.

### Examples

✅ Good
- "Hej, jag heter Gustav. Jag designar och bygger gränssnitt."
- "Hi, I'm Gustav. I design and build interfaces."
- "Selected work, 2021 → now."
- "Send a note" *(button)*
- "Three projects I'm proud of." *(section heading)*

❌ Avoid
- "Welcome to my portfolio!" *(generic)*
- "Innovative design solutions for the modern web." *(buzzword soup)*
- "CLICK HERE TO LEARN MORE" *(shouty)*
- "🚀 Let's build something amazing 🎉" *(emoji as content)*

### Emoji & punctuation

- **Emoji: avoid.** The brand has its own playful element (Patrick Hand
  + the brush mark). Emoji compete with that and feel generic. Excepted:
  one carefully-placed emoji is OK in informal contexts (a personal
  newsletter signoff). Never as bullets or icons.
- **Em dash, en dash, ellipsis** — used naturally. Not as decoration.
- **Arrows** — `→` is on-brand for transitions and links ("Read more →").
  Use the unicode glyph, not "->".

---

## VISUAL FOUNDATIONS

### Mood

Dark, warm-neutral, technical-but-handmade. The page is a black sheet
of paper; type is warm off-white ink (`#F0EFE8`); the brush mark is
where the human shows up.

### Color

**One palette — Ember — with light + dark modes.** The default is
dark; add `data-theme="light"` on `<html>` (or any wrapper) for light
mode:

```html
<html data-theme="dark">   <!-- default -->
<html data-theme="light">
```

Token **names never change** — only values — so every component
reflows automatically. `--color-red` / `--color-blue` are kept as
aliases for `--color-accent` / `--color-link` so older components keep
working. Live preview: `preview/palette-explorer.html`.

**Ember — coral accent + teal link, on a light neutral-grey scale.**
Neutrals anchored on the brand owner's greys (`#5F615F`, Pantone Cool
Gray 9 C).

| Role | Token | Dark | Light |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Page background | `--color-bg` | `#242425` | `#F4F4F3` |
| Surface / card | `--color-surface` | `#2E2E30` | `#FFFFFF` |
| Surface raised | `--color-surface-2` | `#38383A` | `#ECECEB` |
| Border | `--color-border` | `#4E4E50` | `#DEDEDC` |
| Text | `--color-text` | `#F2F1EF` | `#1C1B1A` |
| Text muted | `--color-text-muted` | `#B3B1AD` | `#66645F` |
| Accent (coral) | `--color-accent` | `#FF582D` | `#E8431B` |
| Link (teal) | `--color-link` | `#3AA59C` | `#1E8077` |

Coral accent = Pantone 17-1363 TSX. Use color **sparingly**. Most of
the page is `--color-bg` + `--fg1`. The accent is reserved for: the
brush mark, the active nav state, a single hover/CTA, and selection.
The link color is reserved for inline links and focus rings. Never
gradients between them.

### Type

- **Display + body:** Montserrat Variable. Bold (700) for headlines,
  Regular (400) for body, Semibold (600) for UI labels.
- **Hand:** Patrick Hand. Tiny doses — annotations, hand-written
  callouts, a signature-style flourish next to a heading. Never for
  body copy.
- **Mono:** system mono stack. For code, technical metadata
  ("0100 0111"), and timestamps.

Headings use **tight tracking** (`-0.02em`). Eyebrows use **wide
tracking** (`0.12em`) and uppercase. Body has zero tracking.

### Backgrounds

- **Solid `--color-bg` by default.** No gradients. No mesh. No noise.
- **Allowed:** the portrait or a project hero image full-bleed inside
  a generous frame. The image is treated as a window cut into the
  black sheet — never edge-to-edge with the viewport on desktop;
  always with at least `--sp-7` of breathing room.
- **The brush mark** (from the logo) appears as an oversized,
  low-opacity decorative element behind hero sections. ~5–8% opacity,
  red or off-white, never both.

### Spacing

4px base scale (`--sp-1` … `--sp-10`). Layouts breathe. Default
section padding is `--sp-8` (64px) on mobile, `--sp-9` (96px) on
desktop. Don't crowd.

### Borders

- 1px hairline, `--color-border`. That's it.
- Strong borders (`--color-border-strong`) only on focused inputs.
- No double borders. No outline+border combos.

### Corner radii

- `--r-xs` (4px) — inline chips, code.
- `--r-sm` (8px) — buttons, inputs.
- `--r-md` (12px) — cards.
- `--r-lg` (16px) — modals, large feature cards.
- `--r-pill` — pill nav, tags.

### Shadows / elevation

Three steps. Black, soft, never colored except `--shadow-glow-red` /
`--shadow-glow-blue` for accent CTAs (rare). Inset shadows: not used.

### Hover & press states

- **Hover:** lift via `transform: translateY(-1px)` + slightly lighter
  background (`--color-surface-2` → `--color-surface-3`). Color shift
  on accents (`--color-red` → `--color-red-hover`). Underline-on-hover
  for plain links is fine; default link is already underlined.
- **Press:** `transform: translateY(0) scale(0.98)`. No color flash.
- **Disabled:** `opacity: 0.45`, `cursor: not-allowed`.

### Animation

- Default duration: **200ms**. Fast: 120ms. Slow: 400ms (page
  transitions).
- Default easing: `cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)` (ease-out, gentle).
- Springy easing reserved for the brush mark and for the hand-drawn
  Patrick Hand accents on entry.
- **No bounces** on UI controls. No parallax. Restraint is the brand.

### Transparency & blur

- Used **only** on overlays (modal scrim: `rgba(14,14,15,0.6)` +
  `backdrop-filter: blur(8px)`).
- Never on cards. Never on nav.

### Imagery

Black-and-white photography is the default (see the portrait). Color
photos are allowed if they're the work itself. Avoid stock. Avoid
warm filters. Grain is welcome.

### Layout

- **Single column on mobile**, 12-column grid on desktop with a max
  content width of **1120px**. Hero / portrait sections can break the
  grid full-bleed but text always lives in the grid.
- Asymmetric layouts encouraged for case studies. Don't be afraid of
  whitespace on the right.
- Sticky nav at top, transparent over hero, solid `--color-bg` on
  scroll.

### Cards

- Background: `--color-surface`.
- Border: 1px `--color-border`.
- Radius: `--r-md`.
- Padding: `--sp-5` to `--sp-6`.
- Shadow: none by default. `--shadow-md` on hover.

---

## ICONOGRAPHY

The brand mark is itself a **playful hand-drawn paintbrush** — that
sets the tone. Icons elsewhere should feel made-by-a-person, not
sterile.

### Approach

- **System:** [Lucide](https://lucide.dev) via CDN. Lucide's stroke is
  warm, slightly imperfect, and pairs well with Montserrat.
  - Stroke width: **1.75px** (default 2px feels too engineered).
  - Default size: **20px** in UI, **24px** in hero contexts.
  - Color: inherits `currentColor`. Use `--fg1` or `--fg2`.
- **Brand icon:** the brush mark from the logo, used as a recurring
  motif. It's the "0100" half of the logo isolated — see
  `assets/logo-black.png` / `logo-white.png`.
- **Hand-drawn accents:** Patrick Hand can be used to create
  text-as-icon moments — a circled word, an arrow drawn with `→`,
  a "made with ♥" footer note. Use in place of, not in addition to,
  Lucide icons.

### CDN snippet

```html
<script src="https://unpkg.com/lucide@latest"></script>
<i data-lucide="arrow-right"></i>
<script>lucide.createIcons();</script>
```

### Substitution flag

⚠ Lucide is a **substitution** — the brand owner did not specify an
icon set. If a different set (Phosphor, Heroicons, custom) is
preferred, swap the CDN reference and the stroke widths above.

### Emoji & unicode

- Emoji: **no**, except as occasional ironic punctuation in informal
  contexts.
- Unicode arrows (`→`, `↗`, `↘`) and dashes (`—`) are encouraged as
  inline glyphs.

